# What the Repository does not Carry.
#
# `.canonignore` Says what the repository Carries but does not Teach.
# This Says what it never Carries at all.

# Vendor Entrances. Every one of them Resolves to `.agents/`, which is
# the canonical source and Lives in its own repository. An entrance
# committed here is a second copy waiting to Drift.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
.github/agents/
.github/skills/
CLAUDE.md
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.aider*

# Vendored and Generated. Present on Disk, Written by no one here.
node_modules/
vendor/
third_party/
target/
.mvn/
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
go.sum
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
uv.lock
poetry.lock

# The Artefacts this repository Builds, and the tooling it Fetches.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# What Python Leaves behind.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
